Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 18 34 CLINICAL DATA  FNA  Left breast adenocarcinoma    CA on right  May  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  FORMING SEVERAL MASSES AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The carcinoma grows as several masses in the inferior half of the breast  The largest foci spans 5 0cm and at least 2 2cm  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SEPARATELY SUBMITTED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrgen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a 22 x 21 x 4cm left breast  with a suture designating the superior margin  There is an overlying  20 x 12cm  tan ellipse of skin with an unremarkable nipple areola complex  No gross scars or abnormalities are noted on the skin ellipse  Sectioning through the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  well delineated  hard  focally gritty  white pink mass located in the lower  inner quadrant  coming within 2 0cm of the deep resection margin  The tumor is located 5 5cm from the inferior margin  9 5cm from the superior margin  4 0cm from the medial margin  and 15cm from the lateral margin  The mass comes within 1 0cm of the nearest skin margin  with no gross involvement of the nipple  The mass is surrounded by a moderate amount of dense  white  fibrous tissue  1 5cm inferomedial to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  firm nodule  F   The remaining parenchyma is composed predominantly of irregular  white  dense nodules of fibrous tissue with minimal areas of cystification measuring up to 0 5cm in greatest dimension  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm attached axillary tail from which multiple  rubbery lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Section code  A  Tumor in relation to deep margin B C  Tumor in relation to closest skin margins and uninvolved nipple D E  Representative sections of gritty tumor F  Nodule adjacent to tumor G  Representative central section of firm  fibrous tissue H  Representative section from upper outer quadrant displaying cystic structure I J  Firm areas from lower outer quadrant K N  Representative lymph node Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  highest axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  rubbery  firm lymph nodes that is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette O  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  HIGHEST NODE    EXCISION   report_end  , Inferolateral_IMF_(inframammary_fold).
