_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Note  Although the two large nodules of carcinoma have similar morphologic features  they are clearly separate from one another grossly and have associated ductal carcinoma in situ  favoring that they are two separate primary tumors  The smaller foci of invasive carcinoma are also associated with ductal carcinoma in situ and with lymphatic invasion  in one focus   Therefore these too may represent independent primaries  or  in the case of the one focus associated with lymphatic invasion  may have arisen from intra mammary spread of tumor  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  calponin and heavy chain myosin support the absence of myoepithelial cells in one of the small foci of invasive carcinoma  slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and Factor VIII antigen confirm the presence of lymphatic invasion  The tumor cells contain abundant clear to eosinophilic granular cytoplasm  however PAS stain with and without diastase digestion are negative for the presence of glycogen SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OUT OF ONE LYMPH NODE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  which is bisected  and submitted in its entirety as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm yellow pink simple mastectomy  with a central 3 7cm circular white skin ellipse  There is a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm everted nipple  The anterior a