e in situ tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  NOTE  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 40 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect  There is an overlying tan white skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm with an eccentrically located unremarkable nipple with no scar grossly appreciated  No axillary tail identified  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm to rubbery ill defined area containing a few cystic structures averaging 0 2cm in diameter and containing a friable thick tan white material  This area is located within the upper outer quadrant coming to 1 7cm from the blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 3 5cm from the posterior  Located 2 0cm inferior to the ill defined fibrotic area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined rubbery lobulated slightly indurated fibrotic area which comes to 3 0cm from the inferior blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 2 0cm from the posterior margin  The parenchyma in between these two ill defined slightly indurated fibrotic areas consist of rubbery pink to white lobulated blue stained fibrous tissue  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consists of tan yellow to white lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Along the periphery  no lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Posterior margin taken adjacent to overlying superior cystic fibrotic area  B  Anterior soft tissue margin taken adjacent to overlying superior cystic fibrotic area  C F  Entire superior  upper outer quadrant  cystic ill defined fibrotic area  G  Parenchyma in between two suspicious areas  H  Posterior margin taken adjacent to inferior lobulated fibrotic area  I  Inferior anterior soft tissue taken adjacent to the inferior lobulated fibrotic area  J L  Ill defined lobulated inferior fibrotic area entirely submitted  M N  Uninvolved parenchyma  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue  REMOVED_CASE_ID  left axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow portion of fibrofatty tissue containing two tan pink rubbery lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm which are entirely submitted for frozen section as FX  1  now as O  The remaining fibrofatty tissue is entirely submitted in cassette P  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  second left axillary sentinel node 12 480   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular portion of tan yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue containing two tan pink rubbery lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm which are entirely submitted for frozen section as FX  2  now as Q  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary tissue   are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm of irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated portio